cacy rationale within the endoscopic technique [Data: Entities (2780, 2779); Relationships (5139)].\"},{\"summary\":\"The injection tool is an accessory guided through the endoscope to deliver the submucosal lift\",\"explanation\":\"An injection tool is described as being guided through an endoscope to inject fluid between the tumor and underlying muscle layer, facilitating removal by creating a lift/separation plane [Data: Entities (2764, 2499); Relationships (5099)].\\n\\nThis establishes a toolchain inside the community: endoscope as the access platform, injection tool as the accessory instrument, and injected fluid as the agent used to create tissue-layer separation—together enabling the ESD/EMR maneuver described [Data: Entities (2499, 2764, 2779, 2780); Relationships (5099, 5139, 5122, +more)].\"}],\"rating\":3.2,\"rating_explanation\":\"The impact severity is low-to-moderate because the community describes standard clinical diagnostic and minimally invasive treatment workflows (endoscopy, ESD/EMR, and related tools) without any provided allegations, misuse, or noncompliance indicators [Data: Entities (1190, 2762); Relationships (4525, 5114, 5122)].\"}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1442, "prompt_tokens": 3235, "total_tokens": 4677, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}